# SEO metadata — verify before changing

The site is **live for indexing** (no sitewide `noindex` in `src/layouts/Layout.astro`). Mistakes to titles, descriptions, robots tags, or URL structure can hurt search visibility.

## Required before any edit

1. **Get explicit user approval** before changing:
   - `<title>` / page `title` passed to `<Layout>`
   - `<meta name="description">` / page `description`
   - `<meta name="robots">` or any `noindex` / `nofollow` directive
   - `<link rel="canonical">`
   - Open Graph or Twitter meta tags
   - JSON-LD structured data in `Layout.astro` or page `<script type="application/ld+json">`

2. **Show a before/after summary** (old value → new value) in your reply so the user can confirm nothing unintended changed.

3. **Do not re-add sitewide or per-page `noindex`** without explicit approval and a deliberate reason (e.g. staging-only pages).

## Post-launch guardrails (do not break indexing)

- Do not add `rel="nofollow"` to internal links.
- Do not add `Disallow` rules in `public/robots.txt` without approval.
- Do not remove or break `@astrojs/sitemap` in `astro.config.mjs` or `sitemap-index.xml` on deploy.
- Do not change URL slugs of live pages without a **301 redirect** plan in `public/_redirects` (Netlify).
- Keep a **unique** `title` and `description` per page; one `<h1>` per page.
- Do not hide keyword text with `display:none` or `visibility:hidden` for SEO (`sr-only` for accessibility is OK).
- No keyword-stuffed blocks of text.

## Do not

- Change metadata “while you’re here” on unrelated tasks.
- Copy the same title or description onto multiple pages.

